  "description": "# LUMA-00 | Fun 001 | Check Guest Ignore Rules\n\n**📋 Ticket:** [Luma guests → Salesforce campaign members](https://brightdata-group.monday.com/boards/8667788707/pulses/13343839880)\n\n---\n\n**TRIGGER:** Called by `Webhook: Luma-to-HubSpot Guest Sync` (first step). Reusable by any Luma / event process.\n\n**PURPOSE:** Decide whether a guest must be ignored (ignore list or blocked country) before any processing.\n\n**FLOW:**\n1. Match email / domain against `marketing.ignore_list` → PostgreSQL\n2. Get active `blocked_countries` → Data table\n3. Ruby: country (input, else Luma registration answers) + ignore decision\n\n**DB / TABLES:** `marketing.ignore_list` (read), `blocked_countries` data table (read)\n**UPSTREAM:** Webhook: Luma-to-HubSpot Guest Sync  \n**DOWNSTREAM:** none\n\n## Important logic\n- `should_ignore` = ignore-list match OR blocked country. `ignore_reason` joins all reasons with ` | `.\n- `registration_answers`: pass a JSON string (array or already-encoded string both work).\n- Caller must stop when `status = Error` or `should_ignore = true`.\n",
